===== astimezone
a bad zone -> "TypeError: tzinfo argument must be None or of a tzinfo subclass, not type 'int'"
two -> 'TypeError: astimezone() takes at most 1 argument (2 given)'
keyword -> ('2000-01-01T05:00:00+00:00', 0, 'UTC', datetime.timedelta(0))
unknown -> "TypeError: astimezone() got an unexpected keyword argument 'tzinfo'"
None -> ('2000-06-01T00:00:00-04:00', 0, 'EDT', datetime.timedelta(days=-1, seconds=72000))
to its own -> True
to one that is equal -> False
the zone it gives -> ('timezone', "datetime.timezone(datetime.timedelta(days=-1, seconds=72000), 'EDT')")
in winter -> "datetime.timezone(datetime.timedelta(days=-1, seconds=68400), 'EST')"
keeps the microsecond -> 4
the fold goes -> 0
what fromutc() is given -> ('fromutc', '2000-01-01T11:00:00+00:00', True, 'datetime')
   of a naive one -> ('fromutc', '2000-01-01T17:00:00+00:00', True, 'datetime')
   raises -> 'ZeroDivisionError: division by zero'
from one that says nothing -> ('2000-01-01T17:00:00+00:00', 0, 'UTC', datetime.timedelta(0))
   to itself -> 12
now, with it -> (True, 'datetime')
fromtimestamp, with it -> ('fromutc', '1970-01-01T00:00:00+00:00', True, 'datetime')
===== timetuple
dst() gives None -> -1
dst() gives datetime.timedelta(0) -> 0
dst() gives datetime.timedelta(seconds=3600) -> 1
dst() gives datetime.timedelta(microseconds=1) -> 1
dst() gives datetime.timedelta(days=-1, seconds=82800) -> 1
naive -> (-1, None, None, 0)
   before the first -> 'OverflowError: date value out of range'
   after the last -> 'OverflowError: date value out of range'
utctimetuple at the ends -> None
done
